  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#21686\", \"PowerToys#21999\"], \"answer\": \"This feature has been requested before. PowerToys#21686 is the main request, \\\"[Hosts File Editor] Add ability to group entries\\\". It asks for named groups of host entries that you can switch on or off together, such as Local and Live. PowerToys#21999 asked for the same thing and was closed as a duplicate of #21686. PowerToys#20204 also mentions swapping between multiple hosts files, but only as a side suggestion. Nothing in the archive says this is implemented yet, so there is no built-in way to do it today. Upvote and follow #21686, and add your scenarios there (production testing, a QA sandbox, and office versus VPN). Until then, you can toggle each entry's Active switch in Hosts File Editor by hand. You can also restore a saved hosts file from the Hosts File Editor backups.\"}",
